sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin sites page<br/>/admin/sites, AddSiteModal.tsx
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Admin,DB: Covers US 2.0.2. The Add Site flow exists (#153), with name suggestions and a similar-name warning (#162) and boundary selection (#167).<br/>ProtectedRoute requireAdmin hides the page in the browser only. It reads app_metadata in the browser, so it is not a security check.

    Admin->>Page: Select "Add Site" (data-testid add-site-button)
    activate Page
    Page-->>Admin: Open AddSiteModal

    Note over Page,DB: The page loads getProtectedAreaChoices() once. availableProtectedAreas() hides every protected area<br/>that another Site already uses, so one boundary links to one Site.
    Page->>Actions: getSiteSuggestions(), when the modal opens (AT6)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
    Actions->>DB: Read protected_areas (name, folder) and sites_pa.namesite
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Rows
    deactivate DB
    Actions-->>Page: Names in protected_areas that no Site has yet (case ignored)
    deactivate Actions
    Note right of Page: If the call fails, the page shows no suggestions.

    Admin->>Page: Type the Site name
    Page-->>Admin: List the suggestions whose name contains the typed text (at most 8)
    opt Admin selects a suggestion
        Admin->>Page: Select a suggestion
        Page->>Page: Fill the name field with the suggested name
    end
    Admin->>Page: Select a county or "No county"
    Admin->>Page: Search and select a protected area, or leave it empty (AT1)
    Page->>Actions: findSitesWithName(namesite), when the name field loses focus or a suggestion is selected
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
    Actions->>DB: Read every sites_pa.namesite (active, inactive and archived)
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Names
    deactivate DB
    Actions-->>Page: Names that equal the typed name or contain it or are contained in it<br/>(case ignored, the shorter name needs at least 4 characters)
    deactivate Actions
    opt A Site with the same name exists (AT2)
        Page-->>Admin: Show a possible-duplicate warning (add-site-duplicate-warning).<br/>The Admin can still save
    end

    Admin->>Page: Select Save
    Page->>Page: Check the name. It is the only required field. The county is optional
    alt The name is empty (AT3)
        Page-->>Admin: Block creation. Red border on the name, aria-invalid,<br/>and "Site name is required."
    else The name is filled
        Page->>Actions: createSite(namesite, ab_county, protectedAreaId)
        activate Actions
        Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin() reads app_metadata.role<br/>and app_metadata.authenticated from auth.getUser()
        alt Caller is not an Admin, for example a Steward<br/>who sends the request directly (AT4)
            Actions-->>Page: requireApprovedAdmin() throws "Only admins can edit sites."<br/>No Site created
            Page-->>Admin: Show the error in an alert
        else Caller is an Admin
            Actions->>Actions: Trim the name. If empty, throw "Site name is required." (AT3)
            Actions->>Actions: Check that protectedAreaId is null or a positive whole number
            Actions->>DB: Insert sites_pa row (namesite, ab_county, is_active = true, protected_area_id)
            activate DB
            alt Name already exists (23505 on namesite)
                DB-->>Actions: Unique violation
                Actions-->>Page: Error "A site with this name already exists."
                Page-->>Admin: Show the error in an alert. The modal stays open
            else Protected area already linked (23505 on protected_area_id)
                DB-->>Actions: Unique violation
                Actions-->>Page: Error "That protected area is already linked to a site."
                Page-->>Admin: Show the error in an alert. The modal stays open
            else Protected area does not exist (23503)
                DB-->>Actions: Foreign key violation
                Actions-->>Page: Error "The selected protected area does not exist."
                Page-->>Admin: Show the error in an alert. The modal stays open
            else Other insert error
                DB-->>Actions: Error
                Actions-->>Page: Error (error.message or "Failed to create site")
                Page-->>Admin: Show the error in an alert. The modal stays open
            else Insert done
                DB-->>Actions: OK
                Actions-->>Page: OK
                Page->>Actions: getAllSites()
                Actions->>DB: Read sites_pa rows
                DB-->>Actions: Sites
                Actions-->>Page: Sites
                Page-->>Admin: Close the modal. Show the new Site in the list
            end
            deactivate DB
        end
        deactivate Actions
    end
    deactivate Page

    Note over Admin,DB: A new Site is active by default (US 2.0.3 AT5). getSitesOnline reads active Sites, so the new Site<br/>shows in Site search (AT5). The Admin can save after the duplicate warning. The database then refuses an exact duplicate,<br/>because namesite is UNIQUE. The duplicate check ignores case and also matches names that contain each other,<br/>but the UNIQUE constraint does not. sites_pa.protected_area_id links the Site to its boundary in protected_areas<br/>(nullable and unique, migrations 20261009120000 and 20261009120100).
